<item><title>Mozambique police urge calm as ex-presidential candidate Mondlane goes on trial</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mz/mozambique-police-urge-calm-as-ex-presidential-candidate-724005/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mz/mozambique-police-urge-calm-as-ex-presidential-candidate-724005/</guid><category>Mozambique</category><description>Venâncio Mondlane, who leads the ANAMOLA party, faces five charges linked to the post-election protests of late 2024 and early 2025.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:06:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mz/mozambique-police-urge-calm-as-ex-presidential-candidate-724005/share.jpg" length="42272" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mz/mozambique-police-urge-calm-as-ex-presidential-candidate-724005/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
